756" y="287.5" width="135" height="23" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c36" value="A role assignment at any level applies to everything inside that box. Lower levels inherit from higher levels." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=15;fontColor=#1f2933;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5.0" y="501" width="990" height="23" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c37" value="Scope is the set of resources that an assignment applies to. The resources shown are examples." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=14;fontColor=#5f6b7a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="105.5" y="529" width="789" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c38" value="Resources are the fourth level: the items inside a resource group. The root management group is the top of the tree." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=14;fontColor=#5f6b7a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="13.0" y="554" width="974" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>